cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "Hexaform: structured all-hexahedral meshing for natural-shaped inclusions"
message: "If you use Hexaform in published work, please cite it."
type: software
authors:
  - name: "Hexaform contributors"
version: 0.2.0
date-released: "2026-08-23"
license: MIT
abstract: >-
  Hexaform generates conforming, non-voxelated, all-hexahedral
  (HEX8/HEX20/HEX27) finite element meshes of a cuboidal domain containing curved internal
  boundaries, with native Exodus II output. Rather than attempting general
  all-hexahedral meshing, which remains an open problem, it exploits the
  analytic structure of star-shaped inclusions: each inclusion is meshed with a
  cubed-sphere O-grid block inside a macro-box aligned to whole background grid
  cells, so that the block and the background weld exactly and the mesh is
  conforming by construction. Interface nodes lie on the analytic surface to
  machine precision and the residual facet-induced geometric error converges at
  second order. Intended for elastoplastic phase-field fracture models of
  particulate microstructures.
keywords:
  - mesh generation
  - hexahedral mesh
  - Exodus II
  - finite element method
  - phase-field fracture
  - representative volume element
  - cubed sphere
